# OS/7 desktop (GNOME) — amd64 only.
#
# GNOME is here because GUI mode REQUIRES it: supported Microsoft Intune
# enrollment needs GNOME (README, "Identity"). arm64 is server-only and gets no
# desktop list at all.
#
# It ships in the live image so the installer can lay it down OFFLINE when the
# operator picks GUI mode; headless is then a package-removal step, per README's
# one-shared-package-base-per-architecture rule.
#
# NOTE: the desktop is NOT here for the installer's benefit. os7-setup is a
# keyboard-driven TEXT-MODE installer (installer/SETUP-PLAN.md) and needs no
# desktop session - that is precisely why it replaced Calamares, which as a Qt
# GUI app could never have installed the desktop-less arm64 image.
#
# IMPORTANT: live-build package lists do NOT support trailing inline comments.
# Every token on a non-comment line is passed to apt as a package name.
# (docs/BUILD-NOTES.md #9)
#
# NOTE: no Microsoft packages here. The Microsoft APT repos do not exist yet
# during the package-list pass - they are added by hook 0010, so anything from
# them must be installed in a later hook. (docs/BUILD-NOTES.md #10)

ubuntu-desktop-minimal
gnome-shell
gdm3
nautilus
gnome-terminal

# --- Installer ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately no installer package. os7-setup is authored by OS/7 itself
# (C#/.NET, text mode) and is not an archive package. See
# installer/SETUP-PLAN.md. Calamares was removed on 2026-08-23.

# The "familiar feel" extensions (dash-to-panel taskbar, ArcMenu start menu) are
# deliberately absent: neither has a GNOME-50-compatible build in the resolute
# archive. Hook 0070 logs this gap rather than failing the build.
